From af0ad7caada712883dd30f7a5e375b95523a7b0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:56:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Put an A-Z strip above every library listing

Scrolling is the only way through a library listing today: it pages 50 at a time,
so the far end of the alphabet is dozens of loads away, and the search box matches
anywhere in a name so it cannot stand in for one.

Every library view gains a strip under its toolbar - the whole alphabet visible at
once, led by '#' for the top of the listing, where the names that start with a
digit and the ones that reduce to nothing already sort. Picking a letter asks the
server to start the listing there; the letters after it are still below, so
scrolling carries on into them rather than stopping at the end of a bucket.

The strip marks where the listing begins. It does not yet follow the scroll: list
view is virtualised and panel view is not, so tracking the topmost visible item
needs two different mechanisms, and that is worth its own change rather than a
fragile one bolted on here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VpS6zTXcRdworxLZ6Dp1De
